*   **style_aggression_rating**: VXR styling includes aggressive bumpers, air intakes, prominent spoiler, twin Remus exhaust, large 18-inch gloss black wheels, black grille/mirrors, unique rear diffuser. Described as "one mean Corsa", "aggressive front splitter", "sporty but trendy effect". Score: 0.70.
*   **style_modernity_rating**: Corsa D design (2006-2014) with VXR styling. Looks dated compared to the current facelifted model. Score: -0.50.
*   **handling_rating**: Features Bilstein-developed chassis, lowered suspension, Drexler mechanical limited-slip differential. Described as having "unbeatable traction", "hyper-alert front end", "sort of grip that wouldn't disgrace the proverbial littoral mollusc", "can feel really wonderful on a tight, twisty B-road", "will amaze you with how quickly and competently it can dissect a corner". However, the LSD causes significant torque steer ("tugging the steering wheel with every provocation", "steering wheel never stops tugging at your wrists", "battle to keep it going straight"). Score: 0.50.
*   **ride_comfort_rating**: Bilstein-tuned chassis and lowered suspension. Described as "very compromised", "riding a pogo stick", "very firm", "a little firm". Score: -0.50.
*   **cabin_noise_rating**: A lot of wind and road noise once you built up speed. Score: -0.20.
*   **shift_smooth_rating**: 6-speed manual, described as having a "short-shifting lever which is an absolute joy to use" (Corsa E VXR, likely similar to Clubsport). Score: 0.50.
*   **steering_feel_rating**: Power-assisted steering. Described as having an "unpleasant stiction just off centre", lacking precise feedback, "tugging at your wrists" due to LSD, but also "very good steering" and "direct and accurate". Score: 0.00.
*   **adas_score**: Includes ABS, ESP Plus, Traction Control, Hill Start Assist, Airbags. Lacks modern ADAS like AEB, LKA. Score: -0.50.
*   **visibility_rating**: 3-door body style can hinder visibility. Score: -0.10.
*   **headlight_rating**: Chrome-Style Dual Ellipsoidal Halogen Headlights with LED Daytime Running Lights. Bi-xenon headlights were optional (part of Plus Pack on Nurburgring, likely similar for Clubsport). Score: -0.20.
*   **security_rating**: Remote Control Central Deadlocking, Security Deadlocks, Electronic Engine Deadlock Immobiliser, Remote Control Ultrasonic Alarm. Basic security for its time, but older Corsas are known targets and scored poorly in Thatcham tests (Group 34 is high risk). Score: -0.50.
*   **screen_in**: Standard was likely a basic radio/CD player (CD30 MP3). Optional Touch & Connect multi-media system with a five-inch touch screen was available. Score: -0.20.
*   **infotainment_ux_rating**: Basic radio interface or optional 5-inch touchscreen system. Simple interface, but optional system described as "intuitive". Score: -0.10.
*   **smartphone_connect_rating**: Optional Touch & Connect system included USB and Bluetooth. Standard CD30 MP3 had Aux-in. Bluetooth connectivity and AUX connection mentioned as standard on some listings. Score: -0.20.
*   **audio_rating**: CD/MP3 CD player/stereo radio, 6 Speakers, Steering wheel mounted audio controls. Score: 0.00.
*   **usb_ports**: Optional Touch & Connect system included USB. USB connection mentioned as standard on some listings. Likely 1 USB port if equipped. Score: -0.50.
*   **comfort_feature_score**: Recaro shell-backed sports front seats (standard), VXR leather steering wheel, sports pedals. Air Conditioning standard. Optional Leather Pack with heated seats. Score: 0.30.
*   **convenience_feature_score**: Cruise Control, Power Assisted Steering, Remote Central Locking, Electric Front Windows, Heated Door Mirrors. Optional Rear Parking Sensors, Optional Heated Steering Wheel. Lacks modern convenience features like cameras as standard. Score: 0.00.
